{title: Like Mount Zion}
{subtitle: Psalms 125:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Those who [Eb]trust in [Gm]the LORD
Are like Mount [F]Zion [Eb]today
It cannot be [Gm]shaken by wind
[Eb]It stands forever [F]strong and bright
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Like [Bb]Mount Zion, we [F]are held
Like [Eb]Mount [Bb]Zion, we are [F]kept
[Gm]Steadfast [F]and se[Bb]cure [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [Bb]mountains surround Je[Eb]rusalem
So [Gm]the LORD surrounds his [F]people
Both [Eb]now and forever[Gm]more
His care is [Eb]constant and [F]true
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Like [Eb]Mount [Bb]Zion, we are [F]held
Like [Eb]Mount [Bb]Zion, we are [F]kept
[Gm]Steadfast [F]and se[Bb]cure
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [Gm]scepter of [Eb]wickedness
[Bb]Will not rest [F]on the land
Al[Gm]lotted to the right[Eb]eous
So [Bb]they will not [F]reach out
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Do [Eb]good, O LORD, [Gm]to the good
To [Eb]those upright in [F]heart
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Those who turn to [Eb]crooked ways
The [Gm]LORD will lead [F]them away
With the [Eb]evildoers
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Peace be up[Eb]on Is[Bb]rael [Eb]
[Bb]Peace be up[Eb]on Is[Bb]rael
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
